Cell["\<\
The time vector $t^a$ is related to the lapse function \[Alpha] and shift \
vector \[Beta]^i as t^a = \[Alpha] n^a + \[Beta]^a. This allows us to express \
the Lie derivative along $n^a$ in terms of those along $t^a$ and along the \
shift. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.571492023630519*^9, 3.571492193945265*^9}, {
  3.571492413890341*^9, 3.571492414392048*^9}, {3.847290617185779*^9, 
